"Emendation of Bacteroidaceae and Butyrivibrio and Descriptions of Desulfomonas gen. nov. and Ten New Species in the Genera Desulfomonas, Butyrivibrio, Eubacterium, Clostridium, and Ruminococcus | Microbiology Society (https://www.microbiologyresearch.org/content/journal/ijsem/10.1099/00207713-26-2-238)\nciteturn55view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.microbiologyresearch.org/content/journal/ijsem/10.1099/00207713-26-2-238\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 234\nL0: 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: 1887\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Skip to content】\nL5: \nL6: [Input]\nL7: \nL8: 【2†International Journal of Systematic and Evolutionary Microbiology】 【3†Volume 26, Issue 2】\nL9: # Emendation of Bacteroidaceae and Butyrivibrio and Descriptions of Desulfomonas gen. nov. and Ten New Species in the Genera Desulfomonas, Butyrivibrio, Eubacterium, Clostridium, and Ruminococcus 【4†Image: Free】\nL10: \nL11:   * 【5†W. E. C MOORE】^{1}, 【6†J. L. JOHNSON】^{1} and 【7†L. V. HOLDEMAN】^{1}\nL12:   * 【8†View Affiliations Hide Affiliations】\nL13: \nL14: ^{1} 【9†Anaerobe Laboratory, Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University, Blacksburg, Virginia 24061】\nL15: \nL16:   * Published: 01 April 1976\nL17:   * 【8†info Info】\nL18:     * 【10†Article information】\nL19:     * 【11†Full-Text】\nL20:     * 【12†Figures and Tables】\nL21:     * 【13†References (12)】\nL22:     * 【14†Cited By (252)】\nL23:     * 【15†Supplementary Material】\nL24:     * 【16†Metrics】\nL25: \nL26:   * 【8†build Tools】\nL27: ### Tools\nL28: \nL29:     * 【8†Add to my favourites】\nL30: \nL31:     * 【8†Create publication alert】\nL32: \nL33: 【8†Create citation alert】\nL34: \nL35: 【8†Create correction alert】\nL36: \nL37:     * 【8†Export citation】\nL38:       * 【17†BibT_{E}X】\nL39:       * 【18†Endnote】\nL40:       * 【17†Zotero】\nL41:       * 【19†Medlars】\nL42:       * 【20†RefWorks】\nL43:       * 【21†Mendeley†www.mendeley.com】\nL44:     * 【8†Recommend to library】\nL45:     *     * [Input]\nL46: ## Abstract\nL47: The family Bacteroidaceae is emended to include bacteria that are monotrichous or lophotrichous. The genus Butyrivibrio is emended to include lophotrichous bacteria. Desulfomonas, a new genus of nonmotile, nonsporeforming, gram-negative, anaerobic, sulfate-reducing rods, and 10 new species of anaerobes, Desulfomonas pigra, Butyrivibrio crossotus, Ruminococcus gnavus, R. lactaris, R. obeum, Eubacterium dolichum, E. hadrum, E. ramulus, E. siraeum, and Clostridium leptum, are described.\nL48: These species have been isolated from human intestinal contents or from human feces. The type strains of these species are ATCC 29098, 29175, 29149, 29176, 29174, 29143, 29173, 29099, 29066, and 29065, respectively.\nL49:   * Published Online: 01/04/1976\nL50: \nL51: © American Society for Microbiology, 1976\nL52: \nL53: 【22†Image: Loading】\nL54: \nL55: Article metrics loading...\nL56: \nL57: /content/journal/ijsem/10.1099/00207713-26-2-238\nL58: \nL59: 1976-04-01\nL60: \nL61: 2026-11-05\nL62: ## Metrics\nL63: \nL64: 【22†Image: Loading full text...】\nL65: \nL66: Full text loading...\nL67: \nL68: /deliver/fulltext/ijsem/26/2/ijs-26-2-238.html?itemId=/content/journal/ijsem/10.1099/00207713-26-2-238&mimeType=html&fmt=ahah\nL69: \nL70: References\nL71: \nL72:   1. Bryant M. P. 1974 Genus Butyrivibrio,. 420 In Buchanan R. E., Gibbons N. E. Bergey’s manual of determinative bacteriology The Williams and Wilkins Co.; Baltimore:\nL73: 【23†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL74:   2. Bryant M. P., Small N. 1956; The anaerobic mon-otrichous butyric acid-producing curved rod-shaped bacteria of the rumen. J. Bacteriol 72:16–21\nL75: \nL76: 【24†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL77:   3. Holdeman L. V., Good I. J., Moore W. E. C. 1976; Human fecal flora: variation in bacterial composition within individuals and a possible effect of emotional stress. Appl. Environ. Microbiol 31:359–375\nL78: 【25†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL79: 